 # 10\. AI Architecture

 Gemini should not be treated as one giant prompt.

 ComicCraft should use several specialized AI operations.

 ### AI services

```
GeminiService
│
├── generateStory()
├── generateCharacters()
├── generateOutline()
├── generatePanels()
├── generateDialogue()
├── rewriteDialogue()
├── regeneratePanel()
├── continueStory()
└── validateStory()
```

 This makes the application easier to maintain and gives users granular control.

---

 # 11\. Gemini Generation Pipeline

 When the user clicks **Generate Comic**:

```
User Input
    ↓
Input Validation
    ↓
Story Generation
    ↓
Character Generation
    ↓
Story Outline
    ↓
Page Generation
    ↓
Panel Generation
    ↓
Dialogue Generation
    ↓
Story Consistency Check
    ↓
Save to Database
    ↓
Display Comic Editor
```

 For larger comics, the application should avoid sending the entire project blindly to every request. Instead, provide Gemini with the relevant **story bible + current page/panel context**.

