 # 16\. State Management

 The editor has substantial state, so separate it into:

```
Project State
 ├── comic metadata
 ├── characters
 ├── pages
 └── story bible

Editor State
 ├── selected page
 ├── selected panel
 ├── selected character
 ├── zoom
 └── editing mode

AI State
 ├── generating
 ├── operation
 ├── progress
 └── error
```

 A lightweight client-side state solution can be used for editor state, while the database remains the source of truth for saved projects.

