 # 17\. AI Loading Experience

 AI generation may take time, so don't show a generic spinner only.

 Use a creative progress interface:

```
✨ Creating your comic...

✓ Understanding your idea
✓ Building characters
✓ Planning story
● Designing comic panels
○ Writing dialogue
○ Preparing your comic
```

 This makes the wait feel purposeful.

---

 # 18\. Error Handling

 AI applications need explicit failure handling.

 Possible errors:

 - Gemini request failed
- API quota exceeded
- Invalid structured response
- Network failure
- Content rejected
- Database failure
- Export failure

 Example:

```
Something went wrong while creating your comic.

Your existing work is safe.

[ Try Again ]   [ Save Draft ]
```

---

 # 19\. Security Design

 Important rules:

 - Gemini API key stays server-side.
- Validate all user input.
- Validate Gemini output before saving.
- Authenticate project access.
- Users should only access their own projects.
- Sanitize generated HTML/content where necessary.
- Apply reasonable generation limits.
- Don't trust AI-generated IDs or database references.
- Rate-limit expensive AI endpoints.

